-- title:
--   Good-reduction specialization ordinary on the λ-adic eigenplane
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ and a weight-two cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem of $q$-coefficients at primes not dividing $M$ does not occur at any proper divisor of $M$; a prime $\lambda$; a finite set $S\subseteq\mathbb N$ with $\lambda\in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $M$; and $\lambda\nmid M$. Let $O'$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field and $\lambda$ in its maximal ideal, let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms generated by the operators indexed outside $(S\setminus\{\lambda\})$ to $\mathbb C$ sending each $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$) to the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient of $g$, and let $\iota$ map the range of $\chi_g$ into $O'$ so that the image of $T_\lambda$ is a unit. Let $O''$ be a finite local extension of $O'$ of the same type, an algebra over $\mathbb Z_\lambda$, with fraction field $K$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\lambda$ a nonunit of $A$. With the Hecke action `heckeModuleBar M` on $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed modular function field, assume given: a $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-module structure on the Tate module $T_\lambda(J_0(M))$ (sequences $x$ with $x_0=0$, $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$) acting level-wise through $\mathbb Z/\lambda^n$; a Galois representation $\rho_M$ on $O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T_\lambda(J_0(M))$ induced level-wise by the Galois action and adically continuous; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from $\mathbb Z[X_\ell]$ acting through the Hecke action on the second factor; and a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes T_\lambda(J_0(M)))$ of rank two, stable under $\rho_M$, on which each $T_\ell$ ($\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$) and $T_\lambda$ act by the scalars $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$, $\iota(\chi_g(T_\lambda))$, with Frobenius traces on $W$ prescribed by the same scalars. The conclusion is that there is a Hecke-module structure on $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $\mathbb{F}$-modular function field over the residue field $\mathbb F$ of $A$ and a datum $D$ of type `JZeroGoodReductionSpecialization_alt A lam _ M` — a surjective Hecke-equivariant $\mathrm{sp}:J_0(M)\to\mathrm{Pic}^0$ over $\mathbb F$ killing the inertia action, converting Frobenius elements at $\lambda$ into an endomorphism $F$ satisfying $F^2-T_\lambda F+\lambda=0$, and injective on torsion of order prime to $\lambda$ — such that `JZeroOrdConn D W` holds, i.e. $\dim_K(W\cap \operatorname{specKernel} D)\le 1$, where the specialization kernel is the $K$-span of the elements $1\otimes(a\otimes x)$ with $a\in O''$ and $x$ in `specKernelSet D`.
--
--   This is the ordinarity statement at $\lambda$ for the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a newform whose $\lambda$-th eigenvalue is a unit: on the eigenplane the connected part of the reduction of $J_0(M)$ cuts out at most a line. It is used in the construction of the ordinary line inside the eigenplane, via [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_ordLine_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_ordLine_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_not_dvd).
